ses crewing agents and the marine personnel department daily operations; coordinates mariner assignments with properly qualified personnel in accordance with union, industry best-practice and customer contractual requirements; support Program Managers with selection and promotion of best-qualified mariners; represent USMMI during Seafarers Appeals Board hearings and investigate grievance claims; and act as Harassment, Discrimination, Bullying Point of Contact and Designated Employer Representative for USMMI fleet. The position requires a strong command of the USCG mariner qualifications, credentialing process, government contract requirements and must be able to support Company growth as Subject Matter Expert as USMMI bids on new business via the government contracting and commercial processes.", "company_name": "U.S. Marine Management (USMMI)", "last_updated": "2025-04-21T16:26:27.222562", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/u-s-marine-management"}, {"title": "Senior Manager, Marine Personnel", "company": "SubCom", "end_date": "2024-06-01", "company_id": 953160, "department": "Operations", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2019-10-01", "description": "Leading the effective recruitment, crewing and development of marine crews for our fleet of cable vessels in a dynamic and fluid maritime environment. * Hiring, developing and retaining mariner talent of 500+ * International vessel management * Advance scheduling, documentation of mariners on 9 vessels * Managing Crewing Budget * Human Resource - Union Liason", "company_name": "SubCom", "last_updated": "2025-04-21T16:26:27.222562", "highest_level": "manager", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/tyco-electronics-submarine-communications"}, {"title": "Workforce Development and Marine Personnel Manager", "company": "Norfolk Tug Company", "end_date": "2019-10-01", "company_id": 5169228, "department": "", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2014-02-01", "description": "Manage 175 mariners providing logistical support for 18 tug fleet operating along East Coast. Develop and implement training that supports corporate culture while enhancing mariner skill sets. Develop and promote a safety culture within company Point of contact within organization for mariner questions, issues and emergencies. Operating 24/7 in a fluid environment constantly adjusting to changing operational requirements.", "company_name": "Norfolk Tug Company", "last_updated": "2025-04-21T16:26:27.222562", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/norfolk-tug-company"}, {"title": "Researcher and Editor", "company": "Consultant", "end_date": "2014-08-01", "company_id": 1245832, "department": "Education", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2014-01-01", "description": "Respond to client requests for research, editing and reporting on client specified topics, issues and emerging areas of interest. The Middle East Cold War, Looking Glass Publications - October 2015 https://www.scribd.com/doc/283664720/The-Middle-East-ColdWar The Desperate Quest for Humanity: An Update on the Syrian Refugee Crisis, Looking Glass Publications - September 2015 https://www.scribd.com/doc/279016581/The-Desperate-Quest-for-Humanity-An-Update-on-the-Syrian-Refugee-Crisis", "company_name": "Consultant", "last_updated": "2025-04-21T16:26:27.222562", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "Researcher", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/consultant_67"}, {"title": "Complex Crisis and Humanitarian Team Lead, CFC", "company": "NATO Civil Military Fusion Centre", "end_date": "2014-02-01", "company_id": 551968, "department": "", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2011-07-01", "description": "Humanitarian Team Lead  responsible for the planning, research, writing and publishing of Complex Coverage sector.  Supervisory responsibilities over Desk Officers and Interns. Maintenance and development of website database. To accomplish these tasks, the Team Lead conducts extensive research and has interact with a wide array of actors to include; -Civilian and military personnel operating within the crisis area -Representatives from Academia, Think-tanks, and the Independent Organization (IO)/Non-Governmental Organization (NGO) community", "company_name": "NATO Civil Military Fusion Centre", "last_updated": "2025-04-21T16:26:27.222562", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/nato-allied-command-transformation_2"}, {"title": "Program Manager, Executive Education", "company": "George Mason University", "end_date": "2011-07-01", "company_id": 5489, "department": "Education", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2010-04-01", "description": "Consult with a wide variety of business clients to help design and delivery executive education offerings to business clients. Built relationships with GMU faculty in order to more effectively design, plan and implement custom executive education offerings to businesses in the NOVA region.", "company_name": "George Mason University", "last_updated": "2025-04-21T16:26:27.222562", "highest_level": "manager", "sub_department": "Education_administration", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/george-mason-university"}, {"title": "Operations Coordinator", "company": "Search for Common Ground", "end_date": "2010-04-01", "company_id": 20132, "department": "Operations", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2009-04-01", "description": "Responsible for operational support for 22 branch locations worldwide including risk management planning, corporate communications and collection of programme data for assessment. Assist in grant writing, research of funding sources Assist in development of new funding sources", "company_name": "Search for Common 